dered Norman  Dean instead of being punished was  rewarded York upon hearing this decided  that he would return to England raise an  army and get rid of the Kings terrible  advisers which he did two sides had now  formed the Lancastrians led by Somerset  and Queen Margaret who backed the king  and the Yorkists led by Richard of York  tensions remained high for the next  couple of years and in 1452 York was  summoned to meet the king which he  believed was a trap heeeeelp refused to  go and did the only thing he could rebel  by mobilizing an army the King mobilized  in response and both looked poised for  battle  however they stood down York and his  supporters were pardoned who many of  York's opponents were dismissed from  power the next year 1453 was a big year  in English history the early months bore  good news for Henry Gascony was secured  in Queen Margaret became  pregnant this good news wouldn't last  though since the French would bethe  conquer Gascony thus winning the Hundred  Years War to make matters more  complicated there was a feud brewing  between two powerful northern families  the Percy's headed by the Earl of  Northumberland and the Neville's headed  by the Earl of Warwick Somerset sided  with Northumberland and as a result  warrick allied with York it was at this  point that Henry had a mental breakdown  leaving Margaret in charge in October  Margaret gave birth to a son Prince  Edward meaning that York was no longer  the heir to the throne Henry showed no  signs of getting better and in 1454  Regency was established the two factions  fight for power and Parliament gave the  Regency to York York immediately  stripped Somerset of his offices and  sent margaret away from court this  period is known as the first  Protectorate in York was actually a good  region undertaking much needed reform  the king however made a recovery in  later 1454 and soon after removed York  as region and brought Somerset back with  the Lancastrian faction back in control 